# Plant Sensor Simulator

Generates realistic sensor readings for ESP8266/ESP32 devices and sends them to the plant monitoring backend API.

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Start backend (if not running)
cd ../backend && ./vendor/bin/sail up -d

# 2. Seed database (creates device-tokens.json)
cd ../backend && ./vendor/bin/sail artisan db:seed

# 3. Install simulator dependencies
cd ../simulator
pip install -e .

# 4. Configure (copy .env.example to .env and adjust if needed)
cp .env.example .env

# 5. Run simulator once (dry-run to verify payloads)
python -m simulator simulate --once --dry-run

# 6. Run for 1 hour with 5-minute intervals
python -m simulator simulate --interval 5 --duration 60
```

## Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust:

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `SIMULATOR_API_URL` | `http://localhost` | Backend API base URL (no `/api` suffix) |
| `SIMULATOR_TOKEN_FILE` | `../backend/storage/app/private/device-tokens.json` | Path to device tokens |
| `SIMULATOR_VERIFY_SSL` | `true` | Verify SSL certs for HTTPS |
| `SIMULATOR_WS_URL` | *(none)* | WebSocket URL for real-time updates |
| `SIMULATOR_DEFAULT_INTERVAL` | `10` | Minutes between readings |
| `SIMULATOR_DEFAULT_VARIANCE` | `0.15` | Drift factor (±15%) |
| `SIMULATOR_LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Logging level |

## CLI Options

```bash
simulator simulate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -d, --device TEXT       Filter by device serial number
  -i, --interval INT      Minutes between reading batches (default: 10)
  --duration INT          Total minutes to run (0 = infinite, default: 0)
  -v, --variance FLOAT    Drift factor 0.15 = ±15% (default: 0.15)
  --dry-run               Print payloads without sending
  --once                  Send one batch then exit
  --api-url TEXT          Override API base URL
  --token-file TEXT       Override token file path
  --ws-url TEXT           WebSocket URL for real-time updates
```

## Examples

```bash
# Dry run to verify payloads
python -m simulator simulate --once --dry-run

# Run for 1 hour with 5-minute intervals
python -m simulator simulate --interval 5 --duration 60

# Run specific device only
python -m simulator simulate --device ABC123DEF456 --once

# With WebSocket for real-time dashboard updates
python -m simulator simulate --interval 10 --ws-url ws://localhost

# Staging environment
SIMULATOR_API_URL=https://staging-api.example.com python -m simulator simulate --once

# Production (with custom token file)
SIMULATOR_API_URL=https://api.example.com \
SIMULATOR_TOKEN_FILE=/path/to/prod-tokens.json \
python -m simulator simulate --interval 10 --duration 60
```

## Token Provisioning for Hosted Backends

The `device-tokens.json` file is generated by the backend's seeder.

### Option A: Seed on host, copy tokens
```bash
# On hosted server
cd backend && ./vendor/bin/sail artisan db:seed

# Copy to simulator machine
scp user@host:/app/backend/storage/app/private/device-tokens.json ./device-tokens.json

# Run simulator
SIMULATOR_API_URL=https://api.example.com \
SIMULATOR_TOKEN_FILE=./device-tokens.json \
python -m simulator simulate
```

### Option B: Backend token generation command
```bash
# On hosted server or locally against hosted DB
cd backend && ./vendor/bin/sail artisan device:generate-tokens --output=tokens.json

scp user@host:/app/backend/tokens.json ./device-tokens.json
```

## Architecture

```
simulator/
├── src/simulator/
│   ├── cli.py                 # Main entry point (Typer)
│   ├── config/settings.py     # Pydantic settings
│   ├── models/sensor.py       # Sensor bounds, validation, value generation
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── sensor_generator.py  # Gaussian drift / random walk
│   │   ├── http_client.py       # REST API client with retries
│   │   └── ws_client.py         # WebSocket client with auto-reconnect
│   └── commands/simulate.py    # Simulation command logic
├── tests/
├── pyproject.toml
└── .env.example
```

## Sensor Value Generation

Two strategies based on sensor type:

| Strategy | Parameters | Description |
|----------|------------|-------------|
| Gaussian drift | temperature, humidity, ph, water_temperature | Normal distribution around target |
| Random walk | co2, ec, light, water_level | Small steps from previous value |

All values are clamped to backend validation bounds.

